=== inode types and text
empty:     empty
one:       very short file (no magic)
ascii.txt: ASCII text
crlf.txt:  ASCII text, with CRLF line terminators
cr.txt:    ASCII text, with CR line terminators
mixed.txt: ASCII text, with CRLF, LF line terminators
noeol.txt: ASCII text, with no line terminators
long.txt:  ASCII text, with very long lines (400)
utf8.txt:  Unicode text, UTF-8 text
bom.txt:   Unicode text, UTF-8 (with BOM) text
u16le.txt:  Unicode text, UTF-16, little-endian text
u16be.txt:  Unicode text, UTF-16, big-endian text
latin1.txt: ISO-8859 text
ext.txt:    Non-ISO extended-ASCII text
esc.txt:    ASCII text, with escape sequences
over.txt:   ASCII text, with overstriking
bin.dat:    data
dir:        directory
=== scripts and source
s1: POSIX shell script, ASCII text executable
s2: Bourne-Again shell script, ASCII text executable
s3: Bourne-Again shell script, ASCII text executable
s4: Python script, ASCII text executable
s5: Perl script text executable
s6: Node.js script, ASCII text executable
s7: a /opt/odd/interp -x script, ASCII text executable
s8: Python script, Unicode text, UTF-8 text executable
s9: POSIX shell script, ASCII text executable, with CRLF line terminators
c.c:         C source, ASCII text
cpp.cpp:     C++ source, ASCII text
page.html:   HTML document, ASCII text
doc.xml:     XML 1.0 document, ASCII text
pic.svg:     SVG Scalable Vector Graphics image
data.json:   JSON text data
broken.json: ASCII text
run.bat:     DOS batch file, ASCII text, with CRLF line terminators
script.ps1:  PowerShell script, ASCII text
Makefile:    makefile script, ASCII text
cert.pem: PEM certificate
id_key:   OpenSSH private key
=== images
img.png:  PNG image data, 16 x 8, 8-bit/color RGBA, non-interlaced
gray.png: PNG image data, 256 x 64, 1-bit grayscale, interlaced
img.gif:  GIF image data, version 89a, 10 x 20
img.jpg:  JPEG image data, JFIF standard 1.01, aspect ratio, density 1x1, segment length 16, baseline, precision 8, 64x32, components 3
img.bmp:  PC bitmap, Windows 3.x format, 2 x 2 x 24, image size 16, resolution 2835 x 2835 px/m, cbSize 70, bits offset 54
img.ico:  MS Windows icon resource - 1 icon, 16x16, 32 bits/pixel
img.webp: RIFF (little-endian) data, Web/P image, with lossless, 16x8
img.tif:  TIFF image data, little-endian, direntries=1
=== audio and video
snd.wav:   RIFF (little-endian) data, WAVE audio, Microsoft PCM, 16 bit, stereo 44100 Hz
snd.ogg:   Ogg data, Vorbis audio, stereo, 44100 Hz, ~128000 bps
snd.flac:  FLAC audio bitstream data, 16 bit, stereo, 44.1 kHz, 441000 samples
snd.mp3:   MPEG ADTS, layer III, v1, 128 kbps, 44.1 kHz, JntStereo
tag.mp3:   Audio file with ID3 version 2.3.0, contains: MPEG ADTS, layer III, v1, 128 kbps, 44.1 kHz, JntStereo
clip.mp4:  ISO Media, MP4 Base Media v1 [ISO 14496-12:2003]
clip.mov:  ISO Media, Apple QuickTime movie, Apple QuickTime (.MOV/QT)
clip.webm: WebM
=== executables
console.exe: PE32+ executable (console) x86-64, for MS Windows, 2 sections
gui.exe:     PE32+ executable (GUI) x86-64, for MS Windows, 2 sections
lib.dll:     PE32+ executable (DLL) (console) x86-64, for MS Windows, 2 sections
old.exe:     PE32 executable (console) Intel 80386, for MS Windows, 2 sections
managed.exe: PE32 executable (console) Intel 80386 Mono/.Net assembly, for MS Windows, 2 sections
dos.exe:     MS-DOS executable
prog.elf:   ELF 64-bit LSB executable, x86-64, version 1 (SYSV), statically linked
prog.macho: Mach-O 64-bit x86_64 executable, flags:<NOUNDEFS|DYLDLINK|TWOLEVEL|PIE>
Main.class: compiled Java class data, version 52.0 (Java 1.8)
mod.wasm:   WebAssembly (wasm) binary module version 0x1 (MVP)
=== archives and compressed data
p1.gz:    gzip compressed data, from Unix, original size modulo 2^32 12
named.gz: gzip compressed data, was "a.txt", last modified: Tue Nov 14 22:13:20 2023, max compression, from Unix, original size modulo 2^32 0
p2.bz2:   bzip2 compressed data, block size = 900k
p3.xz:    XZ compressed data, checksum CRC64
p4.lzma:  LZMA compressed data, streamed
p5.lzo:   lzop compressed data - version 1.040, LZO1X-1, os: Unix
a.tar:    POSIX tar archive
a.cpio:   ASCII cpio archive (SVR4 with no CRC)
odc.cpio: ASCII cpio archive (pre-SVR4 or odc)
a.a:      current ar archive
a.zip:    Zip archive data, at least v2.0 to extract, compression method=store
old.Z:   compress'd data 16 bits
a.zst:   Zstandard compressed data (v0.8+), Dictionary ID: None
a.7z:    7-zip archive data, version 0.4
a.rar:   RAR archive data, v5
old.rar: RAR archive data, v4
a.cab:   Microsoft Cabinet archive data, 80 bytes, 2 files
=== zip containers
a.jar:     Java archive data (JAR)
a.docx:    Microsoft Word 2007+
a.xlsx:    Microsoft Excel 2007+
a.odt:     OpenDocument Text
empty.zip: Zip archive data (empty)
=== documents and containers
doc.pdf:   PDF document, version 1.7, 3 page(s)
bare.pdf:  PDF document, version 1.4
db.sqlite: SQLite 3.x database, last written using SQLite version 3039004, file counter 2, database pages 2, cookie 0x1, schema 4, UTF-8, version-valid-for 2
app.lnk:   MS Windows shortcut, Item id list present, Points to a file or directory, Has Relative path, Archive, length=1234
setup.msi: Composite Document File V2 Document, MSI Installer
other.ole: Composite Document File V2 Document
disc.iso:  ISO 9660 CD-ROM filesystem data 'WBSH_DISC'
font.ttf:  TrueType Font data, 12 tables
font.woff: Web Open Font Format
